# v0 → LiveView sync

React reference trees live next to the umbrella app:

- `ref/alona-os-ui-design` — last promoted baseline
- `ref/alona-os-ui-design-new` — fresh v0 export to diff against baseline

Phoenix UI: `alona-os-core/apps/alona_ui/lib/alona_ui_web/`

Invoke the workflow with Cursor command **`/sync-v0-ui-to-liveview`** (see `.cursor/commands/sync-v0-ui-to-liveview.md`).

**Visual parity:** the v0 export defines **how the UI should look** (structure, rhythm, chrome). Sync work aims for **side-by-side sameness** with the ref, using Daisy/HEEx as the implementation. Data may differ (no `mock-data` in prod), but **placeholders should still match the ref’s layout** (e.g. same cards, grids, labels). Do not defer visible ref pieces because they import `components/ui/*` — reimplement the same affordances with Phoenix primitives.

## Shell and theme parity (do not skip)

A common mistake is declaring **no LiveView work** after only checking that `layout.tsx` has the same flex structure. v0 separates **sidebar** tokens from **page** tokens.

For every sync (and especially when the diff looks “small”):

1. Read `app/globals.css`: `:root` vs `.dark`, `--sidebar*`, `--background`, and any comment describing the default look (e.g. light-first).
2. Read `app/layout.tsx` and `components/app-sidebar.tsx` (classes on `<aside>`, `body`, theme provider / `defaultTheme`).
3. Compare to `assets/css/app.css` (Daisy themes), `components/layouts/root.html.heex` (early `data-theme` / `localStorage` behavior), and `alona_shell.html.heex` + `nav_item`.

**App frame (see `app/layout.tsx`):** outer `flex h-screen overflow-hidden`; sidebar **`w-56`** when expanded (not `w-64`); right column `flex flex-1 flex-col overflow-hidden`; topbar `h-14 px-4`; **`main`** is the only vertical scroll: `flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto` with page padding equivalent to v0’s `p-6` on route content.

If React shows a **dark nav rail** on a **light** canvas, Phoenix must not use plain `bg-base-100` for the whole aside unless you intentionally want a flat look — match `--sidebar*` (oklch) in CSS variables or equivalent.

If React’s first paint is **light** but Phoenix tracks **OS dark mode** by default, compare theme defaults and `prefers-color-scheme` handling; structural parity is not enough.

**`./scripts/v0-ui-diff.sh`:** only lists files that differ between `ref/alona-os-ui-design` and `ref/alona-os-ui-design-new`. It cannot surface drift between ref and `alona-os-core`, and after a promote you may have no `-new` folder until the next export — the script is not a parity oracle.

**Logo:** v0 sidebar uses a **`w-8 h-8`** mark in the `h-14` logo row (often a letter in a rounded square, not a wide asset). If LiveView uses `logo.svg`, match the **32×32 bounding box** (`h-8 w-8 object-contain`); avoid `h-* w-auto` only, which inflates wide SVGs.

**Topbar:** v0 `app-topbar.tsx` has **no** page title in the header — only left (mode, date, time, weather) and right actions (theme, alerts, Quick Action). Titles like “Command Center” live in **page content** (`h1` in each `page.tsx`). **`alona_shell.html.heex` must not duplicate `page_title` in the bar**; keep `assign(:page_title)` for `<.live_title>` in `root.html.heex` only. Port Quick Action as Daisy `dropdown` + `<.link>`; bell/alerts from `mock-data` still need approval before real wiring.

**`components/ui/**`:** excluded from the **diff script** only. Topbar/page **dropdowns, buttons, sheets** still need a Phoenix equivalent (usually Daisy + `CoreComponents`), not silence.

